  "id": "warning-coloration",
  "term": "warning coloration",
  "definition": "Warning coloration is a biological trait in which an organism becomes more conspicuous, serving as a visual warning to predators. In this source, it is described as evolving because greater conspicuousness can lengthen a predator’s assessment time and reduce mistaken attacks, especially alongside strong chemical defense signals.",
